member.summary:
            Creates a composite view type based on the specified simple view
            interface type.

The composite view may be used to aggregate a series of
            simple views such that they can be treated as a single entity by
            an associated presenter instance. This method caches the newly-
            created type so that subsequent requests for that type are
            appropriately performant.


The dynamically-generated class is equivalent to the
            following, for a simple view type of ISimpleView that exposes
            no additional properties or events beyond those exposed by
            the  interface itself.


            public sealed class ISimpleView__@CompositeView :
            	: CompositeView<ISimpleView>, ISimpleView
            {
            	public SimpleViewModel Model
            	{
            		get
            		{
            			return Views.First().Model;
            		}
            		set
            		{
            			foreach (var view in Views)
            			{
            				view.Model = value;
            			}
            		}
            	}

            	public event EventHandler MyEvent
            	{
            		add
            		{
            			foreach (var view in Views)
            			{
            				view.MyEvent += value;
            			}
            		}
            		remove
            		{
            			foreach (var view in Views)
            			{
            				view.MyEvent -= value;
            			}
            		}
            	}
            }

member.exception:
if type, prefix,
            methodName, returnType or paramTypes is null on entry into the
            method.

member.summary:
            Internal utility method to create a "get" function for the
            specified property type, based on the implementation in the
            specified view type.

The code emitted for this function is roughly equivalent
            to the following:

            	get
            	{
            		return Views.First().PropertyName;
            	}

            Internal utility method to create a "set" function for the
            specified property type, based on the implementation in the
            specified view type.

The code emitted for this function is roughly equivalent
            to the following:

            	set
            	{
            		foreach (var view in Views)
            		{
            			view.PropertyName = value;
            		}
            	}

            Internal utility method to create an "add" function for the
            specified event type, based on the implementation in the
            specified view type.

The code emitted for this function is roughly equivalent
            to the following:

            	add
            	{
            		foreach (var view in Views)
            		{
            			view.EventName += value;
            		}
            	}

            Internal utility method to create a "remove" function for the
            specified event type, based on the implementation in the
            specified view type.

The code emitted for this function is roughly equivalent
            to the following:

            	remove
            	{
            		foreach (var view in Views)
            		{
            			view.EventName -= value;
            		}
            	}
